patches.replacement:
/* DENSITY FIX (home-pace pass, 2026-09-10): this paragraph rendered in
 * the display face at near-headline size, so every stage carried TWO
 * headline-weight lines (.cw-principle__artifact above it, then this)
 * before anything receded. It now uses the body face at .cw-sect-dek's
 * own register -- the site's established "supporting copy" scale -- so
 * the artifact line stays the one thing a scanning eye reads as a
 * headline per stage. color: inherit throughout, no opacity added
 * (CONTRAST FIX above still holds). */
[data-mode="cw"] .cw-principle__text {
  font-family: var(--font-cw-body);
  font-weight: 400;
  font-size: clamp(16px, 1.5vw, 19px);
  line-height: 1.55;
  letter-spacing: normal;
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  max-width: 52ch;
  text-transform: none;
}

[data-mode="cw"] .cw-principle__proof strong {
  font-weight: 600;
  opacity: 1;
}

/* DENSITY FIX (home-pace pass, 2026-09-10): a ledger nested inside a
 * stage was rendering at the exact same weight as the section's own
 * closing "receipts" ledger below it -- full 2px opening rule, 24px row
 * padding, an 18-22px display-weight company name -- so the eye never
 * recedes between "here is the stage" and "here is its proof". Scoped
 * to .cw-principle .cw-ledger only: the closing ledger is a direct
 * child of the section, not of .cw-principle (see the JSX), so it is
 * untouched, and so is every other page -- .cw-ledger/.cw-lrow render
 * nowhere but this one section (grepped). Border reuses the ledger's
 * OWN existing hairline mix (25%, the same token .cw-lrow already uses
 * for its row divider); no new color, no opacity added to text. */
[data-mode="cw"] .cw-principle .cw-ledger {
  margin-top: 18px;
  border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 25%, transparent);
}
[data-mode="cw"] .cw-principle .cw-lrow {
  padding: 16px 0;
}
[data-mode="cw"] .cw-principle .cw-lrow__co {
  font-size: clamp(15px, 1.3vw, 17px);
  font-weight: 500;
}

